  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid genetic‑algorithm‑optimized quantum neural network simulated with 3 qubits to predict stock closing prices using historical data and ~4 million tweets. Across six companies (AAPL, AMZN, GOOG, GOOG‑L, MSFT, TSLA), the model reports R² values between 99.15% and 99.96% with RMSE ranging from 0.30 to 0.61, outperforming several classical and quantum‑inspired baselines in Table 7. However, the quantum component is simulated and very small (3 qubits), so the work does not demonstrate computational quantum advantage.",
